    "description": "A container port with its anchorage. Ships arrive at a steady rate (TEU per day) and wait at anchorage until the berths unload them into the yard, at most the berth capacity per day. During an outage window (outage start <= day < outage end) the berths run at their outage capacity instead. Anchorage wait is the waiting cargo divided by the berth capacity: roughly how many days a newly arriving ship waits. Road and rail shipments take containers from the yard. Time t is in seconds, so every per-day rate is divided by the shared Seconds per day.",
